## WHAT TAILSCALE IS

Tailscale creates a private overlay network (tailnet) using WireGuard tunnels. Key architectural facts:

  Control plane: Tailscale coordination server — exchanges WireGuard public keys, distributes ACLs,
                 handles authentication. Carries virtually no traffic data.
  Data plane:    End-to-end encrypted WireGuard tunnels directly between peers (P2P when possible).
                 DERP relay servers (TCP/443) used only when direct P2P is blocked by NAT/firewall.

  Device private keys NEVER leave the device. The control server only sees public keys.
  If the coordination server goes offline, all existing connections continue working from cached state.

  Every device gets a stable 100.x.y.z Tailscale IP (from the CGNAT range 100.64.0.0/10).
  MagicDNS assigns <hostname>.<tailnet>.ts.net names to each device for human-friendly addressing.

  Default policy: DENY ALL. Every communication path must be explicitly granted.

