## KEY CONCEPTS

### MagicDNS
  Enabled by default. Assigns <hostname>.<tailnet-name>.ts.net to every device.
  Short names (just <hostname>) work within the same tailnet.
  Split DNS: route specific domain queries to internal resolvers.
    Example: internal.example.com → your corporate DNS server
    All other queries → public DNS

### Subnet Routers
  Advertise non-Tailscale subnets into the tailnet without installing Tailscale on every device.
  Requires admin approval (or autoApprovers) before routes are active.
  Advertise: tailscale up --advertise-routes=192.168.1.0/24
  Approve via API: POST /api/v2/device/{id}/routes
    body: {"routes": ["192.168.1.0/24"]}

### Exit Nodes
  Route ALL internet traffic through a specific tailnet device.
  Advertise: tailscale up --advertise-exit-node
  Requires admin approval or autoApprovers.exitNode.
  ACL rule needed: src uses autogroup:internet.

### Auth Keys
  Bootstrap new devices into the tailnet without interactive login.
  Types: reusable/single-use, ephemeral/persistent, preauthorized/manual-approval.
  Tagged keys: device joins with tag identity instead of user identity.
  Ephermal keys: great for CI runners, short-lived containers, k8s pods.

### DERP Relays
  Designated Encrypted Relay for Packets — used when direct WireGuard P2P is blocked.
  TCP/443 TLS. Packets remain end-to-end encrypted even through DERP.
  Tailscale operates global DERP servers. Custom DERP via derpMap in policy file.

### Tailscale Services (Virtual IPs)
  Assign a TailVIP (virtual Tailscale IP) to a logical service across multiple hosts.
  MagicDNS name: svc:<service-name>
  Grant access: use "svc:my-service" as a dst in grants.
  Serve: tailscale serve --service=svc:staging-db --tcp 5432 localhost:5432
  Useful for HA services and services that live inside containers/k3s without static IPs.

